    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "For Sale By Public Auction On Friday 16-October at 2:30pm at The Strand Tavern, Duncannon\r\n\r\nA Unique Coastal Residence On c. 4 Acres In a Truly Spectacular Setting\r\n\r\nFlexible Living Accommodation of c. 128 sq m\r\nBeing Offered in Lots\r\nOutstanding Refurbishment Potential\r\n\r\nRarely does an opportunity arise to acquire a property such as this traditional farmhouse at Ballystraw, Duncannon. Enjoying a wonderfully private setting and standing on approximately 4 acres, the property commands spectacular panoramic coastal views towards Hook Head and across to the Waterford coastline.\r\n\r\nThe farmhouse, which extends to approximately 128 sq m, retains the character and proportions while now requiring refurbishment and modernisation, it offers generous and flexible accommodation with considerable potential to create a truly special home. The adjoining outbuildings and traditional courtyard further add to the appeal and possibilities of the property. The grounds offer a wonderful sense of space and privacy with its elevated position and far-reaching sea views it is a hidden gem.\r\n\r\nConveniently located close to the picturesque village of Duncannon and its Blue Flag beach, the property is ideally positioned for enjoying all that The Hook Peninsula has to offer. The area is renowned for its beaches and coastal walks, together with attractions including Hook Lighthouse and Tintern Abbey. The renowned Aldridge Lodge and Dunbrody Country House Hotel are also close by, while the villages of Arthurstown, Ballyhack and Fethard-on-Sea add to the excellent choice of amenities, restaurants and places to explore throughout this special corner of South Wexford. Ballystraw represents a rare opportunity for those seeking a permanent home or coastal retreat with land, character and exceptional views, and the chance to create something entirely their own. Viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the setting and potential of this unique property.\r\n\r\nThe property is being offered as follows:\r\n\r\nLot 1. The Farmhouse on 0.833ha (2.05 acre)\r\nLot 2. Field 0.78ha (1.92 acre)\r\nLot 3. The Entire\r\n\r\nSolicitor: Paul Murran, Peter O'Connor & Son Solicitors, Wyse House, Adelphi Quay, Waterford\r\n\r\nSERVICES: Septic tank, mains water and O.F.C.H.\r\nBER: E1 No 119160067\r\nEIRCODE: Y34PX98\r\nVIEWING: By prior appointment"
      },
